### `[signal]` void QAction::toggled(bool *checked*)

This signal is emitted whenever a checkable action changes its
[isChecked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop)() status. This
can be the result of a user interaction, or because
[setChecked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop)() was called.
As [setChecked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop)() changes
the [QAction](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html), it emits
[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)() in addition to
toggled().

*checked* is true if the action is checked, or false if the action is unchecked.

**Note:** Notifier signal for property
[checked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop).

**See also**
[QAction::activate](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#activate)(),
[QAction::triggered](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#triggered)(), and
[checked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop).

