    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### autoRepeat : bool\n\nThis property holds whether the action can auto repeat\n\nIf true, the action will auto repeat when the keyboard shortcut combination is held\ndown, provided that keyboard auto repeat is enabled on the system. The default value is\ntrue.\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.2.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **autoRepeat**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setAutoRepeat**(*bool*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#autoRepeat'
    checkable: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### checkable : bool\n\nThis property holds whether the action is a checkable action\n\nA checkable action is one which has an on/off state. For example, in a word processor, a\nBold toolbar button may be either on or off. An action which is not a toggle action is a\ncommand action; a command action is simply executed, e.g. file save. By default, this\nproperty is `false`.\n\nIn some situations, the state of one toggle action should depend on the state of others.\nFor example, "Left Align", "Center" and "Right Align" toggle actions are mutually\nexclusive. To achieve exclusive toggling, add the relevant toggle actions to a\n[QActionGroup](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qactiongroup.html) with the\nQActionGroup::exclusive property set to true.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isCheckable**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setCheckable**(*bool*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[QAction::setChecked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked-prop)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checkable'
    checked: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### checked : bool\n\nThis property holds whether the action is checked.\n\nOnly checkable actions can be checked. By default, this is false (the action is\nunchecked).\n\n**Note:** The notifier signal for this property is\n[toggled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toggled)(). As toggling a\n[QAction](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html) changes its state, it will\nalso emit a [changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)() signal.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isChecked**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setChecked**(*bool*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[toggled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toggled)**(bool *checked*) |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [checkable](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checkable-prop)\nand [toggled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toggled)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#checked'
    enabled: Any
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### enabled : bool\n\nThis property holds whether the action is enabled\n\nDisabled actions cannot be chosen by the user. They do not disappear from menus or\ntoolbars, but they are displayed in a way which indicates that they are unavailable. For\nexample, they might be displayed using only shades of gray.\n\n**What's This?** help on disabled actions is still available, provided that the\n[QAction::whatsThis](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#whatsThis-prop)\nproperty is set.\n\nAn action will be disabled when all widgets to which it is added (with\n[QWidget::addAction](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#addAction)()) are\ndisabled or not visible. When an action is disabled, it is not possible to trigger it\nthrough its shortcut.\n\nBy default, this property is `true` (actions are enabled).\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isEnabled**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setEnabled**(*bool*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [text](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#text-prop).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#enabled"
    font: QFont
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### font : [QFont](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfont.html)\n\nThis property holds the action's font\n\nThe font property is used to render the text set on the\n[QAction](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html). The font will can be\nconsidered a hint as it will not be consulted in all cases based upon application and\nstyle.\n\nBy default, this property contains the application's default font.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QFont | **font**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setFont**(const QFont \\&*font*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[QAction::setText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#text-prop)() and\n[QStyle](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstyle.html).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#font"
    icon: QIcon
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### icon : [QIcon](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qicon.html)\n\nThis property holds the action's icon\n\nIn toolbars, the icon is used as the tool button icon; in menus, it is displayed to the\nleft of the menu text. There is no default icon.\n\nIf a null icon ([QIcon::isNull](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qicon.html#isNull)())\nis passed into this function, the icon of the action is cleared.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QIcon | **icon**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setIcon**(const QIcon \\&*icon*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#icon"
    iconText: str
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### iconText : [QString](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstring.html)\n\nThis property holds the action's descriptive icon text\n\nIf\n[QToolBar::toolButtonStyle](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtoolbar.html#toolButtonStyle-prop)\nis set to a value that permits text to be displayed, the text defined held in this\nproperty appears as a label in the relevant tool button.\n\nIt also serves as the default text in menus and tooltips if the action has not been\ndefined with [setText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#text-prop)() or\n[setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toolTip-prop)(), and will\nalso be used in toolbar buttons if no icon has been defined using\n[setIcon](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#icon-prop)().\n\nIf the icon text is not explicitly set, the action's normal text will be used for the\nicon text.\n\nBy default, this property contains an empty string.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QString | **iconText**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setIconText**(const QString \\&*text*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also**\n[setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#toolTip-prop)() and\n[setStatusTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#statusTip-prop)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#iconText"
    iconVisibleInMenu: Any
    'Qt 5 reference:\n\n### iconVisibleInMenu : bool\n\nThis property holds whether or not an action should show an icon in a menu\n\nIn some applications, it may make sense to have actions with icons in the toolbar, but\nnot in menus. If true, the icon (if valid) is shown in the menu, when it is false, it is\nnot shown.\n\nThe default is to follow whether the\n[Qt::AA\\_DontShowIconsInMenus](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#ApplicationAttribute-enum)\nattribute is set for the application. Explicitly settings this property overrides the\npresence (or abscence) of the attribute.\n\nFor example:\n\n```\nQApplication app(argc, argv);\napp.setAttribute(Qt::AA_DontShowIconsInMenus);  // Icons are *no longer shown* in menus\n// ...\nQAction *myAction = new QAction();\n// ...\nmyAction->setIcon(SomeIcon);\nmyAction->setIconVisibleInMenu(true);   // Icon *will* be shown in menus for *this* action.\n```\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.4.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **isIconVisibleInMenu**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setIconVisibleInMenu**(bool *visible*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n**See also** [QAction::icon](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#icon-prop)\nand\n[QCoreApplication::setAttribute](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#setAttribute)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#iconVisibleInMenu'
    menuRole: Any
    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### menuRole : [MenuRole](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#MenuRole-enum)\n\nThis property holds the action's menu role\n\nThis indicates what role the action serves in the application menu on macOS. By default\nall actions have the\n[TextHeuristicRole](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#MenuRole-enum),\nwhich means that the action is added based on its text (see\n[QMenuBar](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qmenubar.html) for more information).\n\nThe menu role can only be changed before the actions are put into the menu bar in macOS\n(usually just before the first application window is shown).\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.2.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QAction::MenuRole | **menuRole**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setMenuRole**(QAction::MenuRole *menuRole*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **[changed](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#changed)**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#menuRole"
