### void QClipboard::clear([QClipboard::Mode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#Mode-enum) *mode* \\= Clipboard)

Clear the clipboard contents.

The *mode* argument is used to control which part of the system clipboard is used. If
*mode* is
[QClipboard::Clipboard](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#Mode-enum),
this function clears the global clipboard contents. If *mode* is
[QClipboard::Selection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#Mode-enum),
this function clears the global mouse selection contents. If *mode* is
[QClipboard::FindBuffer](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#Mode-enum),
this function clears the search string buffer.

**See also**
[QClipboard::Mode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#Mode-enum) and
[supportsSelection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qclipboard.html#supportsSelection)().

