Pops up a modal color dialog with the given window *title* (or "Select Color" if none is
specified), lets the user choose a color, and returns that color. The color is initially
set to *initial*. The dialog is a child of *parent*. It returns an invalid (see
[QColor::isValid](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcolor.html#isValid)()) color if
the user cancels the dialog.

The *options* argument allows you to customize the dialog.

This function was introduced in Qt 4.5.

