class QFontDialog:
    """PythonQtInstanceWrapper object

Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

A font dialog is created through one of the static
[getFont](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfontdialog.html#getFont)() functions.

Examples:

```
bool ok;
QFont font = QFontDialog::getFont(
                &ok, QFont("Helvetica [Cronyx]", 10), this);
if (ok) {
    // the user clicked OK and font is set to the font the user selected
} else {
    // the user canceled the dialog; font is set to the initial
    // value, in this case Helvetica [Cronyx], 10
}
```

The dialog can also be used to set a widget's font directly:

```
myWidget.setFont(QFontDialog::getFont(0, myWidget.font()));
```

If the user clicks OK the font they chose will be used for myWidget, and if they click
Cancel the original font is used.

![A font dialog in the Fusion widget
style.](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/images/fusion-fontdialog.png)

Source: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfontdialog.html"""

