Processes the event *event*, and dispatches it to the respective event handlers.

In addition to calling the convenience event handlers, this function is responsible for
converting mouse move events to hover events for when there is no mouse grabber item.
Hover events are delivered directly to items; there is no convenience function for them.

Unlike [QWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html),
[QGraphicsScene](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicsscene.html) does not have
the convenience functions
[enterEvent()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#enterEvent) and
[leaveEvent()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#leaveEvent). Use this
function to obtain those events instead.

Returns `true` if *event* has been recognized and processed; otherwise, returns `false`.

