### void QGraphicsWidget::releaseShortcut(int *id*)

Removes the shortcut with the given *id* from Qt's shortcut system. The widget will no
longer receive
[QEvent::Shortcut](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#Type-enum) events for
the shortcut's key sequence (unless it has other shortcuts with the same key sequence).

**Warning:** You should not normally need to use this function since Qt's shortcut
system removes shortcuts automatically when their parent widget is destroyed. It is best
to use [QAction](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html) or
[QShortcut](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qshortcut.html) to handle shortcuts,
since they are easier to use than this low-level function. Note also that this is an
expensive operation.

This function was introduced in Qt 4.5.

**See also**
[grabShortcut](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#grabShortcut)(),
[setShortcutEnabled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#setShortcutEnabled)(),
and
