    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### layout : [QGraphicsLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicslayout.html)\\*\n\nThis property holds the layout of the widget\n\nAny existing layout manager is deleted before the new layout is assigned. If *layout* is\n`nullptr`, the widget is left without a layout. Existing subwidgets' geometries will\nremain unaffected.\n\n[QGraphicsWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/graphicsview.html#qgraphicswidget)\ntakes ownership of *layout*.\n\nAll widgets that are currently managed by *layout* or all of its sublayouts, are\nautomatically reparented to this item. The layout is then invalidated, and the child\nwidget geometries are adjusted according to this item's\n[geometry](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicslayoutitem.html#geometry)() and\ncontentsMargins(). Children who are not explicitly managed by *layout* remain unaffected\nby the layout after it has been assigned to this widget.\n\nIf no layout is currently managing this widget, layout() will return `nullptr`.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| QGraphicsLayout \\* | **[layout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#layout)**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **[setLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#setLayout)**(QGraphicsLayout \\**layout*) |\n\n**Notifier signal:**\n\n| void | **layoutChanged**() |\n| --- | --- |\n\n### [QGraphicsLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicslayout.html) \\*QGraphicsWidget::layout() const\n\nReturns this widget's layout, or `nullptr` if no layout is currently managing this\nwidget.\n\n**Note:** Getter function for property layout.\n\n**See also**\n[setLayout](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#setLayout)().\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgraphicswidget.html#layout"
