    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### layoutDirection : [Qt::LayoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#LayoutDirection-enum)\n\nThis property holds the layout direction for this widget.\n\nThis property modifies this widget's and all of its descendants'\n[Qt::WA\\_RightToLeft](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum)\nattribute. It also sets this widget's\n[Qt::WA\\_SetLayoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum)\nattribute.\n\nThe widget's layout direction determines the order in which the layout manager\nhorizontally arranges subwidgets of this widget. The default value depends on the\nlanguage and locale of the application, and is typically in the same direction as words\nare read and written. With\n[Qt::LeftToRight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#LayoutDirection-enum), the\nlayout starts placing subwidgets from the left side of this widget towards the right.\n[Qt::RightToLeft](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#LayoutDirection-enum) does\nthe opposite \\- the layout will place widgets starting from the right edge moving\ntowards the left.\n\nSubwidgets inherit their layout direction from the parent. Top-level widget items\ninherit their layout direction from QGraphicsScene::layoutDirection. If you change a\nwidget's layout direction by calling setLayoutDirection(), the widget will send itself a\n[LayoutDirectionChange](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#Type-enum) event,\nand then propagate the new layout direction to all its descendants.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| Qt::LayoutDirection | **layoutDirection**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setLayoutDirection**(Qt::LayoutDirection *direction*) |\n| void | **unsetLayoutDirection**() |\n\n**See also**\n[QWidget::layoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#layoutDirection-prop)\nand\n[QApplication::layoutDirection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#layoutDirection-prop