### `[signal]` void QGroupBox::clicked(bool *checked* \\= false)

This signal is emitted when the check box is activated (i.e., pressed down then released
while the mouse cursor is inside the button), or when the shortcut key is typed.
Notably, this signal is *not* emitted if you call
[setChecked](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qgroupbox.html#checked-prop)().

If the check box is checked, *checked* is true; it is false if the check box is
unchecked.

This function was introduced in Qt 4.2.

