class QGuiApplication:
    """PythonQtInstanceWrapper object

Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

QGuiApplication contains the main event loop, where all events from the window system
and other sources are processed and dispatched. It also handles the application's
initialization and finalization, and provides session management. In addition,
QGuiApplication handles most of the system-wide and application-wide settings.

For any GUI application using Qt, there is precisely **one** QGuiApplication object no
matter whether the application has 0, 1, 2 or more windows at any given time. For
non-GUI Qt applications, use
[QCoreApplication](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html) instead, as
it does not depend on the Qt GUI module. For
[QWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html) based Qt applications, use
[QApplication](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qapplication.html) instead, as it
provides some functionality needed for creating
[QWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html) instances.

The QGuiApplication object is accessible through the
[instance](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#instance)()
function, which returns a pointer equivalent to the global
[qApp](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qapplication.html#qApp) pointer.

QGuiApplication's main areas of responsibility are:

- It initializes the application with the user's desktop settings, such as [palette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#palette)(), [font](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#font)() and [styleHints](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#styleHints)(). It keeps track of these properties in case the user changes the desktop globally, for example, through some kind of control panel.
- It performs event handling, meaning that it receives events from the underlying window system and dispatches them to the relevant widgets. You can send your own events to windows by using [sendEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#sendEvent)() and [postEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#postEvent)().
- It parses common command line arguments and sets its internal state accordingly. See the [constructor documentation](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#QGuiApplication) below for more details.
- It provides localization of strings that are visible to the user via [translate](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#translate)().
- It provides some magical objects like the [clipboard](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#clipboard)().
- It knows about the application's windows. You can ask which window is at a certain position using [topLevelAt](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#topLevelAt)(), get a list of [topLevelWindows](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#topLevelWindows)(), etc.
- It manages the application's mouse cursor handling, see [setOverrideCursor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#setOverrideCursor)()
- It provides support for sophisticated [session management](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/ipc.html#session-management). This makes it possible for applications to terminate gracefully when the user logs out, to cancel a shutdown process if termination isn't possible and even to preserve the entire application's state for a future session. See [isSessionRestored](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#isSessionRestored)(), [sessionId](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#sessionId)() and [commitDataRequest](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#commitDataRequest)() and [saveStateRequest](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#saveStateRequest)() for details.

Since the QGuiApplication object does so much initialization, it *must* be created
before any other objects related to the user interface are created. QGuiApplication also
deals with common command line arguments. Hence, it is usually a good idea to create it
*before* any interpretation or modification of `argv` is done in the application itself.

| Groups of functions | |
| --- | --- |
| System settings | [desktopSettingsAware](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#desktopSettingsAware)(), [setDesktopSettingsAware](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#setDesktopSettingsAware)(), [styleHints](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#styleHints)(), [palette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#palette)(), [setPalette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#setPalette)(), [font](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#font)(), [setFont](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#setFont)(). |
| Event handling | [exec](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#exec)(), [processEvents](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#processEvents)(), [exit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#exit)(), [quit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#quit)(). [sendEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#sendEvent)(), [postEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#postEvent)(), [sendPostedEvents](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#sendPostedEvents)(), [removePostedEvents](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#removePostedEvents)(), hasPendingEvents(), [notify](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#notify)(). |
| Windows | [allWindows](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#allWindows)(), [topLevelWindows](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#topLevelWindows)(), [focusWindow](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#focusWindow)(), [clipboard](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#clipboard)(), [topLevelAt](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#topLevelAt)(). |
| Advanced cursor handling | [overrideCursor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#overrideCursor)(), [setOverrideCursor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#setOverrideCursor)(), [restoreOverrideCursor](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#restoreOverrideCursor)(). |
| Session management | [isSessionRestored](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#isSessionRestored)(), [sessionId](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#sessionId)(), [commitDataRequest](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#commitDataRequest)(), [saveStateRequest](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qguiapplication.html#saveStateRequest)(). |
| Miscellaneous | [startingUp](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#startingUp)(), [closingDown](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcoreapplication.html#closingDown)(). |

