### `[virtual]` int QLayoutItem::heightForWidth(*int*) const

Returns the preferred height for this layout item, given the width, which is not used in
this default implementation.

The default implementation returns -1, indicating that the preferred height is
independent of the width of the item. Using the function
[hasHeightForWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlayoutitem.html#hasHeightForWidth)()
will typically be much faster than calling this function and testing for -1.

Reimplement this function in layout managers that support height for width. A typical
implementation will look like this:

```
int MyLayout::heightForWidth(int w) const
{
    if (cache_dirty || cached_width != w) {
        MyLayout *that = const_cast<MyLayout *>(this);
        int h = calculateHeightForWidth(w);
        that->cached_hfw = h;
        return h;
    }
    return cached_hfw;
}
```

Caching is strongly recommended; without it layout will take exponential time.

**See also**
[hasHeightForWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlayoutitem.html#hasHeightForWidth)().

