### void QLineEdit::setCompleter([QCompleter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html) \\**c*)

Sets this line edit to provide auto completions from the completer, *c*. The completion
mode is set using
[QCompleter::setCompletionMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html#completionMode-prop)().

To use a [QCompleter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html) with a
[QValidator](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qvalidator.html) or
[QLineEdit::inputMask](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlineedit.html#inputMask-prop),
you need to ensure that the model provided to
[QCompleter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html) contains valid entries.
You can use the
[QSortFilterProxyModel](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsortfilterproxymodel.html)
to ensure that the [QCompleter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html)'s
model contains only valid entries.

If *c* \\=\\= 0, setCompleter() removes the current completer, effectively disabling auto
completion.

This function was introduced in Qt 4.2.

**See also** [completer](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qlineedit.html#completer)()
and [QCompleter](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcompleter.html).

