### void QMenuBar::clear()

Removes all the actions from the menu bar.

**Note:** On macOS, menu items that have been merged to the system menu bar are not
removed by this function. One way to handle this would be to remove the extra actions
yourself. You can set the [menu
role](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qaction.html#MenuRole-enum) on the different
menus, so that you know ahead of time which menu items get merged and which do not. Then
decide what to recreate or remove yourself.

