### void QMessageBox::setWindowModality([Qt::WindowModality](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowModality-enum) *windowModality*)

This function shadows
[QWidget::setWindowModality](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#windowModality-prop)().

Sets the modality of the message box to *windowModality*.

On macOS, if the modality is set to
[Qt::WindowModal](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowModality-enum) and
the message box has a parent, then the message box will be a
[Qt::Sheet](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WindowType-enum), otherwise the
message box will be a standard dialog.

This function was introduced in Qt 4.2.

