class QPageLayout:
    """PythonQtInstanceWrapper object

Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

The QPageLayout class defines the layout of a page in a paged document, with the page
size, orientation and margins able to be set and the full page and paintable page
rectangles defined by those attributes able to be queried in a variety of units.

The page size is defined by the
[QPageSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpagesize.html) class which can be
queried for page size attributes. Note that the
[QPageSize](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpagesize.html) itself is always defined
in a Portrait orientation.

The minimum margins can be defined for the layout but normally default to 0\\. When used
in conjunction with Qt's printing support the minimum margins will reflect the minimum
printable area defined by the printer.

In the default
[StandardMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpagelayout.html#Mode-enum) the
current margins and minimum margins are always taken into account. The paintable
rectangle is the full page rectangle less the current margins, and the current margins
can only be set to values between the minimum margins and the maximum margins allowed by
the full page size.

In [FullPageMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpagelayout.html#Mode-enum) the
current margins and minimum margins are not taken into account. The paintable rectangle
is the full page rectangle, and the current margins can be set to any values regardless
of the minimum margins and page size.

Source: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpagelayout.html"""

