printing, this resolution refers to the physical printer's resolution. The logical DPI
on the other hand, refers to the resolution used by the actual paint engine.

Note that if the physicalDpiY() doesn't equal the
[logicalDpiY](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpaintdevice.html#logicalDpiY)(), the
corresponding [QPaintEngine](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpaintengine.html) must
handle the resolution mapping.

**See also**
