### bool QPictureIO::write()

Writes an picture to an IO device and returns `true` if the picture was successfully
written; otherwise returns `false`.

Before writing an picture you must set an IO device or a file name. If both an IO device
and a file name have been set, the IO device will be used.

The picture will be written using the specified picture format.

Example:

```
        QPictureIO iio;
        QPicture   picture;
        QPainter painter(&picture);
        painter.drawPixmap(0, 0, pixmap);
        iio.setPicture(picture);
        iio.setFileName("vegeburger.pic");
        iio.setFormat("PIC");
        if (iio.write())
            return true; // returned true if written successfully
```

**See also**
[setIODevice](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpictureio.html#setIODevice)(),
[setFileName](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpictureio.html#setFileName)(),
