### void QStackedWidget::removeWidget([QWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#QWidget) \\**widget*)

Removes *widget* from the
[QStackedWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstackedwidget.html). i.e., *widget*
is *not* deleted but simply removed from the stacked layout, causing it to be hidden.

**Note:** Parent object and parent widget of *widget* will remain the
[QStackedWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstackedwidget.html). If the
application wants to reuse the removed *widget*, then it is recommended to re-parent it.

**See also**
[addWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstackedwidget.html#addWidget)(),
[insertWidget](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstackedwidget.html#insertWidget)(),
