Returns the size hint for the given *row*'s height or -1 if there is no model.

If you need to set the height of a given row to a fixed value, call
[QHeaderView::resizeSection](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qheaderview.html#resizeSection)()
on the table's vertical header.

If you reimplement this function in a subclass, note that the value you return is only
used when
[resizeRowToContents](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtableview.html#resizeRowToContents)()
is called. In that case, if a larger row height is required by either the vertical
header or the item delegate, that width will be used instead.

**See also**
[QWidget::sizeHint](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#sizeHint-prop),
[verticalHeader](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtableview.html#verticalHeader)(),
