class QToolTip:
    """PythonQtInstanceWrapper object

Native bases: PythonQtInstanceWrapper

Supplemental documentation:
Qt 5 reference:

## Detailed Description

The tip is a short piece of text reminding the user of the widget's function. It is
drawn immediately below the given position in a distinctive black-on-yellow color
combination. The tip can be any [rich
text](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtextedit.html) formatted string.

Rich text displayed in a tool tip is implicitly word-wrapped unless specified
differently with `<p style='white-space:pre'>`.

The simplest and most common way to set a widget's tool tip is by calling its
[QWidget::setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#toolTip-prop)()
function.

It is also possible to show different tool tips for different regions of a widget, by
using a [QHelpEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qhelpevent.html) of type
[QEvent::ToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#Type-enum). Intercept
the help event in your widget's
[event()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#event) function and call
[QToolTip::showText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#showText)() with
the text you want to display. The
[Tooltips](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtwidgets-widgets-tooltips-example.html)
example illustrates this technique.

If you are calling
[QToolTip::hideText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#hideText)(), or
[QToolTip::showText](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#showText)() with
an empty string, as a result of a
[ToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#Type-enum)-event you should
also call [ignore()](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#ignore) on the
event, to signal that you don't want to start any tooltip specific modes.

Note that, if you want to show tooltips in an item view, the model/view architecture
provides functionality to set an item's tool tip; e.g., the
[QTableWidgetItem::setToolTip](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtablewidgetitem.html#setToolTip)()
function. However, if you want to provide custom tool tips in an item view, you must
intercept the help event in the
[QAbstractItemView::viewportEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qabstractitemview.html#viewportEvent)()
function and handle it yourself.

The default tool tip color and font can be customized with
[setPalette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#setPalette)() and
[setFont](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#setFont)(). When a tooltip is
currently on display,
[isVisible](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#isVisible)() returns `true`
and [text](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html#text)() the currently
visible text.

**Note:** Tool tips use the inactive color group of
[QPalette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpalette.html), because tool tips are not
active windows.

Source: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtooltip.html"""

