### `[slot]` bool QWidget::close()

Closes this widget. Returns `true` if the widget was closed; otherwise returns `false`.

First it sends the widget a
[QCloseEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qcloseevent.html). The widget is
[hidden](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#hide) if it
[accepts](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#accept) the close event. If it
[ignores](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qevent.html#ignore) the event, nothing
happens. The default implementation of
[QWidget::closeEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#closeEvent)()
accepts the close event.

If the widget has the
[Qt::WA\\_DeleteOnClose](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum)
flag, the widget is also deleted. A close events is delivered to the widget no matter if
the widget is visible or not.

The
