    "Qt 5 reference:\n\n### autoFillBackground : bool\n\nThis property holds whether the widget background is filled automatically\n\nIf enabled, this property will cause Qt to fill the background of the widget before\ninvoking the paint event. The color used is defined by the\n[QPalette::Window](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpalette.html#ColorRole-enum)\ncolor role from the widget's\n[palette](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpalette.html).\n\nIn addition, Windows are always filled with\n[QPalette::Window](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qpalette.html#ColorRole-enum),\nunless the WA\\_OpaquePaintEvent or WA\\_NoSystemBackground attributes are set.\n\nThis property cannot be turned off (i.e., set to false) if a widget's parent has a\nstatic gradient for its background.\n\n**Warning:** Use this property with caution in conjunction with [Qt Style\nSheets](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/stylesheet.html). When a widget has a style\nsheet with a valid background or a border-image, this property is automatically\ndisabled.\n\nBy default, this property is `false`.\n\nThis property was introduced in Qt 4.1.\n\n**Access functions:**\n\n| bool | **autoFillBackground**() const |\n| --- | --- |\n| void | **setAutoFillBackground**(bool *enabled*) |\n\n**See also**\n[Qt::WA\\_OpaquePaintEvent](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum),\n[Qt::WA\\_NoSystemBackground](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#WidgetAttribute-enum),\nand [Transparency and Double\nBuffering](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#transparency-and-double-buffering).\n\nSource: https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwidget.html#autoFillBackground"
