### `[virtual]` bool QWizardPage::validatePage()

This virtual function is called by
[QWizard::validateCurrentPage](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwizard.html#validateCurrentPage)()
when the user clicks **Next** or **Finish** to perform some last-minute validation. If
it returns `true`, the next page is shown (or the wizard finishes); otherwise, the
current page stays up.

The default implementation returns `true`.

When possible, it is usually better style to disable the **Next** or **Finish** button
(by specifying [mandatory
fields](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwizard.html#mandatory-fields) or
reimplementing
[isComplete](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwizardpage.html#isComplete)()) than to
reimplement validatePage().

**See also**
[QWizard::validateCurrentPage](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwizard.html#validateCurrentPage)()
and [isComplete](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qwizardpage.html#isComplete)().

